{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789224230,"nonce":"EvqvEBQwrHo+7+WIwK1FJWm3lsE=","title":"MIR-level inlining before type specialisation","message":"Inlining happens at Cranelift lowering by splicing the callee's unspecialised MIR, so an inlined body's arithmetic keeps its inline number guards and boxing, and a callee's own loops or calls cannot inline at all (single-block bodies only). Ash inlines in AIR before its middle end, so the caller's known types flow into the callee. Do the same: after devirtualisation produces CallKnownFunc sites, substitute small callee bodies into the caller's MIR (fresh value ids, block params mapped to args, the call replaced by the return value), then run the JIT pipeline so TypeSpecialize sees the whole thing. Requires moving devirt ahead of build_compile_mir, which the inline-cache realignment already supports.","files":null}]}